  "note": "Card heights in CSS pixels at the width above. Keyed by COMPONENT, one entry per card: two cards over the same ds-docs section render different slices of it and are different heights. The Design System pane sizes a card from the `viewport` in its @dsCard marker and clips anything taller, so a missing number silently cuts the bottom off a page. GENERATED - run `node .design-sync/tools/measure-cards.mjs`, which serves the built upload tree and loads every card in an iframe tall enough that nothing scrolls, then reads the `.ds-page` div's offsetHeight. It measures the real card files rather than re-deriving what a card renders, because a card slices itself in its own inline script and a second copy of that logic drifts - the hand pass this replaced measured whole sections while the cards had already started slicing. Do not read documentElement.scrollHeight: it floors at the frame height, which once reported a 167px card as 200. Verified frame-independent: the same numbers come back in an 848px frame and a 2848px one.",
